
    Inheritance is an Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) concept that allows one class to acquire the properties (variables) and behaviors (methods) of another class.
    It promotes code reusability, extensibility, and represents an IS-A relationship.


Constructor in Inheritance

    When a child object is created
     new Dog();

    Java first executes

    Animal() -> then Dog()

    Reason -> Parent must initialize first.

    Execution

    Main()

    ↓

    Dog Object

    ↓

    Animal()

    ↓

    Dog()

    ↓

    Program Continues

Constructor Chaining

Definition

    Automatic calling of parent constructors before child constructors.

    Keyword - super();

    Example :

        Animal()

            ↓

        Dog()

            ↓

        Puppy()

